3 1 Northern Border Alliance Program; Reporting Requirements. Amend RSA21-P:69, IV to read
4 asfollows:
5 IV. The program shall include semi-annual reporting, tothe governor, senate president, and
6 speaker of the house of representatives, which includes measurable program results and a detailed
7 accounting of program funding and uses. Any grants provided to state, county, or local law
8 enforcement agencies in accordance with the intentions of the program shall be reported,
9 including who received such grants, when, and what the funds were used for. The number
10 of personnel involved in the program as well as their rank and/title shall be included in
11 the report. Any equipment or technology used and purchased through the program shall
12 also be included. The report shall also include the number of persons arrested, persons
13 cited, and persons subjected to a field stop or warning. The report shall also include the
14 date, time, and location of Customs and Border Protection-related incidents, assists,
15 intelligence received, or other activity. For persons in each of these categories, the
16 aggregate data shall also include the municipality and country where each such person
17 resides. For persons who are arrested or cited, the report shall also include the race of
18 such persons to the extent such information is indicated on the complaint, summons, or
19 citation. ThefirstreportshallbesubmittedonorbeforeDecember31,2023.
